    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d349">

                <pb facs="0697" n="573" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg573"/>

                <head>No. 345.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Evarts to Sir Edward
                        Thornton.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-12-02"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 2,
                        1880</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that I have
                    received a letter from my colleague, the Secretary of the Interior, in which he
                    says that <pb facs="0698" n="574" xml:id="pg574"/> it has been represented to
                    him that there is a trading establishment located at Woody Mountain in the
                    Dominion of Canada, about 30 miles from the north line of the Blackfeet
                    Reservation, Fort Beck Agency, Montana Territory, which is a rendezvous for
                    robbers and murderers, and a point from which arms and ammunition are supplied
                    to Indians who are hostile to this country.</p>
                <p>In view of the grave character of the complaints in regard to this matter which
                    have reached this government from sources deemed to be entirely trustworthy, I
                    feel it to be my duty to lose no time in bringing this subject to your
                    attention, in order that Her Majesty’s Government may cause inquiries to be made
                    into the facts of the case, so that, if the representations made to the
                    Secretary of the Interior, above referred to, shall be ascertained to be well
                    founded, prompt action for the remedy of the evil complained of may be taken by
                    the Canadian authorities.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WM. M. EVARTS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
